## Source progress — 2026-11-10: typed local MIF serialization

`makeAwdlChannelSixMif` now constructs the four required outbound MIF TLVs
(synchronization, simple channel sequence, Election-v2 and Version) using
bounded, typed caller-supplied fields. The frame advertises channel 6 only
in explicitly selected 2.4-GHz slots and zero otherwise, without claiming
an unsupported 5-GHz radio capability. It rejects invalid station/master
addresses, absent social slots, invalid MIF countdowns, wrapped MAC
sequence and unsafe output aliases before modifying caller-owned output.
The independent source parser and neighbor-state machinery round-trip
these frames in a synthetic host fixture, including valid copied election,
synchronization and channel state plus buffer/field rejection. Both
C++14 and C++17 ASan+UBSan and focused strict Clang-Tidy/format pass.

All timestamp, metric, sequence and channel-slot values require independent
native owner evidence. The serializer is not called by a macOS AWDL host,
BLE discovery, radio scheduler or TX queue. Apple peer election, service
policy, RF coexistence, authenticated IPv6 and AirDrop transfer remain
unimplemented; this P0 TODO is still open.

## AWDL ingress address guard — 2026-11-10

`parseAwdlAction` rejects action frames with an all-zero destination as
`InvalidAddress`, matching the outbound action serializer and IPv6 ingress
policy. The malformed frame never becomes a peer observation. A synthetic
regression keeps the otherwise valid MIF body intact to prove this rejection;
focused Clang-Tidy, format and C++14/C++17 ASan+UBSan pass. This is only
input validation, not peer authorization or native AWDL readiness.

