## Source progress — 2026-11-10: common channel-six rendezvous

`planSharedAwdlChannelSixRendezvous` intersects independently stamped local
and neighbor MIF channel-six schedules. Both must advertise a complete
three-TU-guarded window for the same airtime; disjoint phases never inherit
permission from an otherwise valid peer-only candidate. It searches at most
two candidates per EAW during the two five-second anchors, returns the local
and peer AW sequences and channel slots at the shared start, and bounds its
reported usable duration by both synchronization expiries. Aliased outputs,
clock rollback, stale MIF samples, invalid addresses, impossible airtime and
monotonic-timestamp overflow fail closed.

Synthetic regressions cover current/future overlaps, disjoint slot cycles,
independent MIF phase anchors, exact five-second expiry, timestamp overflow
and duration clipping. These are source-only calculations and do not connect
the MAC to any macOS AWDL interface, operating channel, Bluetooth discovery,
coexistence lease, DMA transmission or AirDrop peer trust. The P0 TODO remains
open; real timestamps and actual radio TX authorization still require native
integration.
